    passage: 'Cold nights tax the energy reserves of small hummingbirds, which lose heat rapidly and cannot feed in darkness; studying 249 hummingbirds along an elevational gradient in the Colombian Andes, ecologists Diana Carolina Revelo Hernández, Justin Baldwin, and Gustavo Londoño determined that smaller individuals were especially likely to enter torpor at low temperatures.',
