    passage: 'The hypothesis that the Homeric poems emerged from an oral tradition might seem impossible to evaluate, since no recordings of ancient bards survive. Milman Parry argued, however, that the tradition is clearly ______ the poems’ language itself, in recurring formulaic expressions, such as conventional epithets for divinities and heroes, that accommodate the meter and that performers could readily reuse.',
